313
00:55:49,612 --> 00:55:53,612
Like with any diet, veganism comes with benefits and growbacks.

314
00:55:54,612 --> 00:56:07,612
Although veganism can be a healthy, sustainable diet for some, it's important to learn about any potential risks associated with this popular eating pattern before choosing to adhere to it.

315
00:56:08,612 --> 00:56:25,612
To begin with, vegan diets tend to be rich in many nutrients, low in cholesterol, but there are many nutrients that those following a vegan diet, oftentimes do not consume enough.

316
00:56:26,612 --> 00:56:36,612
If you aren't careful, following a vegan diet can cause you to develop some deficiencies in calcium and omega-3 fatty acids.

317
00:56:36,612 --> 00:56:46,612
These deficiencies can impact your body in a variety of ways, possibly causing you to have a weakened immune system.

318
00:56:47,612 --> 00:56:57,612
What is more concerning is not getting enough vitamin D, the so-called sunshine vitamin, which is important for our bones and teeth.

319
00:56:57,612 --> 00:56:58,612
If you do not include it to your diet, there is a higher risk of experiencing broken bones.

320
00:56:58,612 --> 00:57:10,612
Another concern about vegan dieting is soy consumption.

321
00:57:10,612 --> 00:57:16,612
As vegans exclude all forms of animal protein, they turn to soy as a protein source.

322
00:57:16,612 --> 00:57:29,612
However, scientific studies show that processed forms of soy may cause high blood pressure and therefore can increase the risk of heart disease.

323
00:57:29,612 --> 00:57:35,612
Moreover, there is data that only 20% of soy worldwide is organic.

324
00:57:35,612 --> 00:57:46,612
So, if you are consuming too much, no organic soy regularly, it might lead to harmful effects on your overall health in the long run.

325
00:57:46,612 --> 00:58:00,612
All in all, there are disadvantages associated with veganism, since those who do not eat a balanced and varied diet usually have a weakened state of health than meat eaters.

326
00:58:00,612 --> 00:58:01,612
This is the suggested summary.

327
00:58:01,612 --> 00:58:13,612
In her article, Being Wigan, Janet Tuscan explains some potential drawbacks for following a vegan diet.

328
00:58:13,612 --> 00:58:33,612
Since vegans abstain from consumption of any food that comes from animals, their diet lacks certain nutrients which leads to vitamin deficiencies, and in the end, this ongoing state of deficiency may manifest as weak immunity and bone diseases.

329
00:58:33,612 --> 00:58:39,612
Another danger that comes with vegan lifestyle is related to soy consumption.

330
00:58:39,612 --> 00:58:52,612
Weigans are highly dependent on soy protein instead of animal protein, but overconsumption of this process and no organic food can be detrimental to vegans' health.

